Exception:


NOTE: Some modifier key combinations will not work in the Unity Editor, but they will work in a game build.

This happens if the external function throws an exception. This could indicate the error is in your code if Rewired is calling a function in an interface implementation you created. Read the exception message and the stack trace carefully to find the source of the exception being thrown.

This can also happen if you forget to unsubscribe to an event in a MonoBehaviour class and that object gets destroyed.

Exception:


This happens if your event handler/callback code throws an exception. This means the error is in your code, not Rewired. Read the exception message and the stack trace carefully to find the source of the exception being thrown by your code.

This can also happen if you forget to unsubscribe to an event in a MonoBehaviour class and that object gets destroyed. Make sure you unsubscribe to events in OnDisable or OnDestroy. Rewired will attempt to continue running.

