This warning does not mean that Rewired will not function, but it may not function optimally.

Some different major versions of Unity download Asset Store assets to the same folder location on disk, so if you download an asset in one version of the Unity editor, then open another version of the Unity editor and install the asset without re-downloading it, the wrong asset version will be installed. To fix this, manually re-download Rewired in the Unity Asset Store panel in this version of the Unity Editor, then install it.

If you are using a beta version of a new major version of Unity, you will have to wait until the release of the final version before a compatible version of Rewired can be uploaded to the Asset Store. When the new version is ready, it will be available through the Unity Asset Store for download as usual.. . Attempting to retry.... Cannot assign Custom Controller to Player.. Failed to cache catalog to location . Final Point Size: . No receiver for uri . Please install Rewired for Unity . Serializing self referenced value.. Skipping serializing self referenced value.. There are . This element should be renamed to a unique name.. Unable to delete cache data from location . Will skip rendering. You can create Actions in the editor.. You may be hitting Unity's vertex count limit (.'.*[a-zA-Z]+.*.*[bB]+.*.*[pP]+.*........, .//.0.0.0b0.Array..Array.data[.Array.size.Experimental.UIElements.GetSchema() must have an Id..U2022.UIElements.asset.bat.bundle.cctor.cloudfunctions.net/.com.config.ctor.database.chinacloudapi.cn.database.cloudapi.de.database.usgovcloudapi.net.database.windows.net.dll.exe.fonts.hash.json.local.m_FileID.mono.rem.try.xsd.{8}//*///=/>/Applications/Date(/configuration/system.runtime.remoting/etc/localtime/etc/terminfo/lib/terminfo/photos/posts/posts/1/proc/settings.json/system/lib/liblog.so/system/lib64/liblog.so/todos/users/usr/compat/linux/proc/usr/lib/terminfo/usr/share/usr/share/templates/usr/share/terminfo/usr/share/zoneinfo/00

